From 495d619981430fdfdaf2922311ef8408a7f34943 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeanluca <jeanlucafp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:12:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(login): refuse a duplicate account login as the legacy
 server
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A second login of an account already in character selection or play was
accepted: both sessions shared the account, SetCargo replaced the live
cargo with the stored copy, and the first session's teardown evicted the
cargo the other one still used. The fire-and-forget teardown saves also
let a new login load rows older than the previous session's state.

Follow the legacy (DBSrv CFileDB.cpp:1001-1017, TMSrv _MSG_DBSavingQuit):
the session already in the game gets _NN_Your_Account_From_Others and is
closed (which saves it), and the new login gets _MSG_StillPlaying (0x011D,
new constant); the 7662 client shows "Conexão anterior finalizada. Tente
novamente." While that save is in flight a retry gets _MSG_AlreadyPlaying
(0x011C), so it never reloads stale rows. The refused session returns to
UserAccept and may retry on the same connection (also for the dbServer
ALREADY_PLAYING branch, which used to leave it in UserLogin).

removeSession now saves the character and cargo through
saveAccountOnClose, which counts the account as saving until both saves
return to the loop (worldCallbackEvent), still under saveWG for shutdown.
The check is per tmServer: the dbServer does not track online accounts.

Tests: kick + refusal + retry, retries refused while the save is blocked,
kick from play saves the character, other accounts unaffected. Handler
tests that put two players in the world with the same account now log the
extra ones in as "tester#N" aliases (same character, distinct account) and
retry a login refused while the previous session closes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
